# DAPS WordPress Template — Prod Caddy Config
# This file is imported by the root DAPS Caddyfile on the remote VM.
# Caddy will automatically obtain and renew a TLS certificate for your domain.
#
# SETUP: Replace "mywpsite.example.com" with your actual domain name.
# Caddy requests the certificate when it starts, and Let's Encrypt only issues it once
# your domain's DNS A record points at your server. For a new site, add that record
# before deploying. When moving a live site, deploy first and flip DNS after — see
# "DNS and HTTPS" in daps/docs/readme-deployment.md.
#
# www: If you want www.yourdomain.com to work, add a DNS A record for it too,
# then add a redirect block below. Caddy will obtain a separate certificate for it.

mywpsite.example.com {
	encode gzip zstd
	reverse_proxy mywpsite:80
}

# www.mywpsite.example.com {
# 	redir https://mywpsite.example.com{uri} permanent
# }
